  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">INSTITUTIONALIZING COMMUNITY-BASED MANAGEMENT OF ELEPHANT CONFLICT AND STRENGTHENING MANAGEMENT OF DANDELI ELEPHANT RESERVE BY PARTNERSHIP WITH FOREST DEPARTMENTS AND LOCAL SELF-GOVERNANCE BODIES, KAR</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE GOAL OF THIS PROJECT IS TO INSTITUTIONALIZE AND STRENGTHEN A PARTICIPATORY MODEL OF MANAGING HUMAN-ELEPHANT CONFLICT IN THE NORTH KARNARA SOUTHERN MAHARASHTRA LANDSCAPE BY EMPOWERING LOCAL FARMERS TO PROTECT THEIR CROPS USING SIMPLE, LOW-TECH SOLUTIONS AND TO IMPLEMENT SOUND MANAGEMENT PRACTICES IN DANDELI ELEPHANT RESERVE AND SOUTHERN MAHARASHTRA, INDIA. PROJECT OBJECTIVE AND ACTIVITIES ARE TO: (1) INSTITUTIONALIZE THE COMMUNITY-BASED CONFLICT MANAGEMENT IN VILLAGE FOREST COMMITTEES AND ECO-DEVELOPMENT COMMITTEES OF THE FOREST DEPARTMENT USING A PARTICIPATORY RURAL APPRAISAL PROCESS IN 80 NEW VILLAGES (2) INTRODUCE TECHNOLOGY-BASED SOLUTIONS FOR HEC MANAGEMENT INCLUDING AN INFRARED SENSOR-BASED ELEPHANT ALERT SYSTEM, SOLAR FLICKER LIGHTS, AND USE OF A SMARTPHONE APP PREVIOUSLY DEVELOPED WITH US FISH AND WILDLIFE SERVICE FUNDING (3) USE AN SMS ALERT SYSTEM TO RECEIVE AND SEND ALERTS OF ELEPHANT PRESENCE IN VILLAGES (4) IDENTIFY INDIVIDUAL ELEPHANTS USING PHOTOGRAPHIC CAPTURE-RECAPTURE METHODOLOGY AND UNDERTAKE AN ANALYSIS OF POPULATION SIZE (5) PREPARE A MANAGEMENT PLAN FOR DANDELI ELEPHANT RESERVE BASED ON MAPPING LAND USE, POTENTIAL FOR ALTERNATIVE CROPS, SURVEYS LOCAL RESIDENTS OF PERCEPTION OF ELEPHANT CONSERVATION, AND CONSULTATIONS WITH FOREST DEPARTMENT OFFICIALS AND FRONTLINE STAFF (6) SUPPOR</narrative>
  </description>
